# Copy this file to `.env` IN THIS DIRECTORY and fill in a key.
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# It has to live in backend/, not the project root. config.py declares
# `env_file=".env"` as a relative path, so pydantic-settings resolves it against
# the current working directory -- and the documented way to start the server is
# `cd backend && python main.py`. A .env at the project root is read only if you
# also launch from there, which is why a misplaced one fails silently: no error,
# the planner just quietly falls back to heuristic buckets.
#
# `.env` is gitignored. This example file is not -- keep it free of real keys.

# --- LLM key --------------------------------------------------------------
# One of these is enough. Gemini is the default; a free key comes from
# https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- Web search -----------------------------------------------------------
# Optional. Without any provider the web_search tool says so plainly and agents
# answer from model knowledge, marking the output as unverified.
#
# Searches are tried in order: TAVILY_API_KEY, then TAVILY_API_KEY_FALLBACK,
# then Jina. A provider that refuses is skipped for the rest of the process and
# the next one answers, so one spent key no longer ends research for the run --
# which is what happened on 2026-09-21, when a key hit its 1,000-search plan
# limit and two missions researched with a tool returning no URLs at all.
#
# The server prints what each key has left at startup, so an exhausted key is
# visible in the first second rather than mid-mission.
#
# Free tier is 1,000 searches/month, no card: https://app.tavily.com
# TAVILY_API_KEY=
# A key on a second account, for when the first runs out mid-mission.
# TAVILY_API_KEY_FALLBACK=
# SEARCH_DEPTH=basic
#
# The last resort, and it needs no new credential: s.jina.ai searches on the
# same JINA_API_KEY the reader fallback uses. Set false to keep search
# first-party to Tavily.
# JINA_SEARCH_ENABLED=true

# --- Optional overrides ---------------------------------------------------
# Anything in config.py's Settings can be overridden here. Shown with the
# defaults it already uses, so uncommenting changes nothing until you edit it.

# DEFAULT_MODEL=gemini/gemini-2.5-flash
# FALLBACK_MODEL=gemini/gemini-2.0-flash
# TEMPERATURE=0.2

# Guardrails worth knowing about on a first real run: MAX_AGENT_STEPS caps the
# ReAct loop so a confused agent cannot spin forever, and PLANNER_TIMEOUT is how
# long the DAG request may take before falling back to the heuristic buckets.
# MAX_AGENT_STEPS=8
# PLANNER_TIMEOUT=20.0
# PARALLEL_ENABLED=true
